From 6bb09a6c42284a52d06b10e4104e5334250fefa6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alessandro Fontana <alessandro.fontana@pm.me>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 15:50:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 189/191] thermal: thermal-generic-adc: no IIO channel without
 #io-channel-cells

The driver registers its temperature as an IIO channel for other drivers
to read, on every node. A node without #io-channel-cells cannot be
referenced by an io-channels property, so nothing in the kernel consumes
that channel there; it only reaches userspace, where Android's IIO
sensors HAL enumerates in_temp_input and reports the battery thermistor
of the Galaxy Tab A 10.1 (2016) as an ambient temperature sensor.

Register the channel only when the node declares #io-channel-cells.

---
 drivers/thermal/thermal-generic-adc.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/thermal/thermal-generic-adc.c b/drivers/thermal/thermal-generic-adc.c
index 7c844589b1..2de870e8b8 100644
--- a/drivers/thermal/thermal-generic-adc.c
+++ b/drivers/thermal/thermal-generic-adc.c
@@ -206,6 +206,16 @@ static int gadc_thermal_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 
 	devm_thermal_add_hwmon_sysfs(dev, gti->tz_dev);
 
+	/*
+	 * The temperature is offered to other drivers as an IIO channel, but a
+	 * node nobody can reference (no #io-channel-cells) has no consumer:
+	 * there the channel only reaches userspace, where Android's IIO
+	 * sensors HAL takes a battery thermistor for an ambient temperature
+	 * sensor.
+	 */
+	if (!of_property_present(pdev->dev.of_node, "#io-channel-cells"))
+		return 0;
+
 	return gadc_iio_register(&pdev->dev, gti);
 }
 
